From: lane 3 <lane3@ios-nord>
Subject: [PATCH] a6xx: flush the CCU before the first framebuffer-reading draw


A draw that reads the framebuffer reads it through UCHE, and FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP only orders
such draws among themselves. The first one after a draw that did not read reads another
tile's pixels (a label's shadow over icons, on a642l: the first triangle of each quad wrong).
Taken from HackiOS's patch; not yet seen on an a620.

---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
@@ -445,6 +445,17 @@
        DRAW == DRAW_INDIRECT_OP_INDIRECT_COUNT)
       ctx->batch->barrier |= FD6_WAIT_FOR_ME;
 
+   /* A draw that reads the framebuffer reads it through UCHE. FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP orders such
+    * draws among themselves, but knows nothing of the draws before the mode was on: the first
+    * triangle to read the framebuffer after one that did not, read the pixels of another tile
+    * (a label's shadow over icons, in CoreAnimation, on a642l: the first triangle of each quad
+    * wrong, the second right). A CCU colour flush mends it -- an UCHE invalidate alone also
+    * does; the first such draw gets both, as a framebuffer barrier would give.
+    */
+   if (unlikely(emit.fs->fb_read) && !ctx->batch->prev_draw_read_fb)
+      ctx->batch->barrier |= FD6_FLUSH_CCU_COLOR | FD6_INVALIDATE_CACHE;
+   ctx->batch->prev_draw_read_fb = emit.fs->fb_read;
+
    if (ctx->batch->barrier)
       fd6_barrier_flush<CHIP>(ctx->batch);
 

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h
@@ -136,6 +136,9 @@
    /* Driver specific barrier/flush flags: */
    unsigned barrier;
 
+   /* the last draw emitted read the framebuffer (see fd6_draw.cc) */
+   bool prev_draw_read_fb;
+
    /* A calculated "draw cost" value for the batch, which tries to
     * estimate the bandwidth-per-sample of all the draws according
     * to:
